        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44696</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44696"/>
        <updated>2026-07-13T16:20:48.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19549634?u=386f7d3a43a7d4b6159b6bbf86a36c79c0586601&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Summary</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #44640.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4809089090" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44640" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/44640/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44640">#44640</a></p>
<p dir="auto">The Example section on the <code class="notranslate">&lt;use&gt;</code> page says it draws "a circle with a different fill and stroke color," and the last copy sets <code class="notranslate">stroke="red"</code>. But the referenced <code class="notranslate">#myCircle</code> already set <code class="notranslate">stroke="blue"</code>, and a <code class="notranslate">&lt;use&gt;</code> copy cannot override a presentation attribute that the referenced element already defines, so the red was ignored and the circle rendered blue.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Change</h3>
<p dir="auto">Remove <code class="notranslate">stroke="blue"</code> from the referenced circle so the <code class="notranslate">stroke="red"</code> on the last copy renders, matching what the surrounding text describes. The attribute-override behavior is still explained in the Usage notes section, so nothing is lost.</p>]]></content>
